1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,008
An earthquake, huh? What's today's video about? It's on disaster preparedness.

2
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Earthquake in Kyushu

3
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:13,641
Good morning.

4
00:00:13,665 --> 00:00:16,149
Good morning.

5
00:00:16,172 --> 00:00:19,790
Did you watch the news on TV this morning?

6
00:00:19,813 --> 00:00:23,447
No, I haven’t seen it yet.

7
00:00:23,470 --> 00:00:26,036
Was there something happening?

8
00:00:26,059 --> 00:00:31,143
There was a big earthquake in Kyushu this morning.

9
00:00:31,167 --> 00:00:34,001
What? Really?

10
00:00:34,024 --> 00:00:36,399
Around what time?

11
00:00:36,422 --> 00:00:39,556
Around 6 AM.

12
00:00:39,579 --> 00:00:43,379
I was still asleep at that time.

13
00:00:43,401 --> 00:00:46,484
We didn’t feel any shaking here, did we?

14
00:00:46,508 --> 00:00:50,575
No, we were fine here.

15
00:00:50,598 --> 00:00:53,849
Was the earthquake in Kyushu strong?

16
00:00:53,872 --> 00:00:58,146
Yes, it was a very strong earthquake.

17
00:00:58,170 --> 00:01:00,981
Were there any injuries?

18
00:01:01,005 --> 00:01:05,972
Yes, there was a woman crying on the news.

19
00:01:05,996 --> 00:01:08,729
That’s terrible.

20
00:01:08,752 --> 00:01:11,602
Is the town okay?

21
00:01:11,626 --> 00:01:15,393
Some old houses were slightly damaged.

22
00:01:15,416 --> 00:01:19,749
I see. Did a tsunami hit?

23
00:01:19,772 --> 00:01:23,972
No, there was no tsunami.

24
00:01:23,995 --> 00:01:26,628
Oh, that’s a relief.

25
00:01:26,651 --> 00:01:30,549
Japan really has so many earthquakes, doesn’t it?

26
00:01:30,573 --> 00:01:33,906
I’m always scared.

27
00:01:33,929 --> 00:01:37,420
Yes, earthquakes are quite common in Japan.

28
00:01:37,444 --> 00:01:42,417
I called my family in my home country this morning.

29
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:45,646
Were they worried?

30
00:01:45,669 --> 00:01:49,436
Yes, they were very concerned.

31
00:01:49,459 --> 00:01:51,525
I can imagine.

32
00:01:51,548 --> 00:01:54,482
Do you have any friends in Kyushu?

33
00:01:54,505 --> 00:01:57,505
No, I don’t.

34
00:01:57,528 --> 00:02:01,661
I have a college friend in Kyushu.

35
00:02:01,684 --> 00:02:03,650
Are they okay?

36
00:02:03,673 --> 00:02:06,446
Should I call them right away?

37
00:02:06,470 --> 00:02:10,365
Yes, I’ll send them an email later.

38
00:02:10,388 --> 00:02:19,397
You can download today’s video script from the description and top comment. Please leave a comment before downloading!

39
00:02:19,397 --> 00:02:20,897
Scene 2: Rest and Reassurance

40
00:02:20,897 --> 00:02:23,190
Good work today.

41
00:02:23,213 --> 00:02:25,284
Let’s take a short break.

42
00:02:25,307 --> 00:02:27,787
Yes, let’s do that.

43
00:02:27,811 --> 00:02:30,244
Would you like some coffee?

44
00:02:30,268 --> 00:02:32,753
Yes, I’d love some.

45
00:02:32,776 --> 00:02:35,343
Thank you as always.

46
00:02:35,366 --> 00:02:39,499
The earthquake in Kyushu this morning was really strong, wasn’t it?

47
00:02:39,522 --> 00:02:43,408
Yes, it was truly powerful.

48
00:02:43,432 --> 00:02:46,299
I was shocked when I saw the news.

49
00:02:46,322 --> 00:02:50,014
Do you have family or friends in Kyushu?

50
00:02:50,037 --> 00:02:54,372
Yes, my parents live in Kyushu.

51
00:02:54,395 --> 00:02:57,239
What? Your parents?

52
00:02:57,262 --> 00:02:59,801
Have you called them yet?

53
00:02:59,824 --> 00:03:03,429
Yes, I called them first thing this morning.

54
00:03:03,453 --> 00:03:06,419
Are your parents okay?

55
00:03:06,442 --> 00:03:09,176
Yes, they're fine.

56
00:03:09,198 --> 00:03:11,532
They were both in good spirits.

57
00:03:11,555 --> 00:03:15,121
That's great to hear.

58
00:03:15,144 --> 00:03:18,811
Yeah, hearing their voices really put me at ease.

59
00:03:18,834 --> 00:03:22,367
Were your parents injured at all?

60
00:03:22,390 --> 00:03:25,678
No, they weren't hurt.

61
00:03:25,702 --> 00:03:28,702
Was everything inside the house okay?

62
00:03:28,725 --> 00:03:31,525
A few dishes broke.

63
00:03:31,548 --> 00:03:35,281
But nothing major.

64
00:03:35,304 --> 00:03:39,504
Do they have enough water and food?

65
00:03:39,527 --> 00:03:42,102
Yes, they have plenty.

66
00:03:42,125 --> 00:03:45,742
My parents always keep water stocked.

67
00:03:45,766 --> 00:03:48,173
That's really smart of them.

68
00:03:48,196 --> 00:03:50,069
That’s reassuring.

69
00:03:50,093 --> 00:03:53,873
But my mom seemed a little tired.

70
00:03:53,896 --> 00:03:56,935
She didn’t sleep much last night either.

71
00:03:56,958 --> 00:04:01,492
Yeah, earthquakes really take a toll on you.

72
00:04:01,515 --> 00:04:05,090
I was so worried too.

73
00:04:05,113 --> 00:04:09,379
Have you contacted your nearby friends yet?

74
00:04:09,402 --> 00:04:12,672
Yes, my friends are all okay.

75
00:04:12,696 --> 00:04:14,263
That’s a relief.

76
00:04:14,286 --> 00:04:17,303
My family is in Tokyo.

77
00:04:17,326 --> 00:04:20,770
Tokyo gets earthquakes a lot too, doesn’t it?

78
00:04:20,794 --> 00:04:25,474
Yeah, so I’ll call my family later.

79
00:04:25,497 --> 00:04:28,097
That’s a good idea.

80
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:30,413
I saw the news.

81
00:04:30,437 --> 00:04:33,416
They said it’s going to rain in Kyushu soon.

82
00:04:33,439 --> 00:04:35,849
What? Really?

83
00:04:35,873 --> 00:04:38,144
That’s dangerous.

84
00:04:38,168 --> 00:04:41,168
Yeah, I’m really worried.

85
00:04:41,191 --> 00:04:44,470
I’ll message my parents again tonight.

86
00:04:44,494 --> 00:04:47,027
Please do.

87
00:04:47,050 --> 00:04:54,155
The link to review today’s video is in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

88
00:04:54,155 --> 00:04:55,655
Scene 3: How to Protect Yourself During an Earthquake

89
00:04:55,655 --> 00:05:01,934
Hey, what would you do if a big earthquake hit right now?

90
00:05:01,958 --> 00:05:06,625
Uh, I’d rush outside as fast as I could.

91
00:05:06,648 --> 00:05:09,181
That’s actually dangerous.

92
00:05:09,204 --> 00:05:12,405
Don’t panic and run outside.

93
00:05:12,428 --> 00:05:14,100
Oh, I see.

94
00:05:14,124 --> 00:05:17,813
So what should I do inside the room?

95
00:05:17,836 --> 00:05:21,474
First, protect your head.

96
00:05:21,497 --> 00:05:23,497
Got it.

97
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:27,120
Use a bag or cushion to shield your head.

98
00:05:27,144 --> 00:05:31,838
Then, get under a table right away.

99
00:05:31,862 --> 00:05:34,695
Under the table, right?

100
00:05:34,718 --> 00:05:36,156
Got it.

101
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:40,460
Hold onto the table legs tightly.

102
00:05:40,484 --> 00:05:41,567
Okay.

103
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:44,801
Should I wait until the shaking stops?

104
00:05:44,824 --> 00:05:47,304
Yes, that's right.

105
00:05:47,327 --> 00:05:51,061
After the shaking stops, turn off the fire.

106
00:05:51,084 --> 00:05:54,851
What should you do if you're cooking when it happens?

107
00:05:54,874 --> 00:05:57,912
Should you turn off the fire immediately?

108
00:05:57,935 --> 00:06:02,738
During a big quake, it's dangerous to be near the stove.

109
00:06:02,761 --> 00:06:05,761
So, when *should* you turn it off?

110
00:06:05,784 --> 00:06:10,017
After the shaking stops, please turn it off.

111
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:11,607
Got it.

112
00:06:11,630 --> 00:06:15,163
First, protect yourself.

113
00:06:15,186 --> 00:06:17,043
Exactly.

114
00:06:17,067 --> 00:06:20,906
Then, open the door to your room.

115
00:06:20,929 --> 00:06:23,900
Why do we need to open the door?

116
00:06:23,923 --> 00:06:28,257
Because after an earthquake, the door might get stuck.

117
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:30,013
I see.

118
00:06:30,036 --> 00:06:33,048
That way, you create an escape route.

119
00:06:33,072 --> 00:06:34,682
Right.

120
00:06:34,705 --> 00:06:39,072
Also, don’t go near the windows.

121
00:06:39,095 --> 00:06:41,895
The glass might shatter.

122
00:06:41,918 --> 00:06:43,416
Okay.

123
00:06:43,439 --> 00:06:46,039
Stay away from the windows.

124
00:06:46,062 --> 00:06:47,865
Got it.

125
00:06:47,888 --> 00:06:50,971
Where should you keep your shoes?

126
00:06:50,995 --> 00:06:55,668
Place slippers or shoes near your bed.

127
00:06:55,691 --> 00:06:59,458
There might be broken glass on the floor.

128
00:06:59,481 --> 00:07:00,914
Okay.

129
00:07:00,937 --> 00:07:03,385
Protect your feet.

130
00:07:03,409 --> 00:07:07,814
I’ll put my shoes near my bed tonight.

131
00:07:07,837 --> 00:07:11,204
Keep your phone nearby too.

132
00:07:11,227 --> 00:07:12,827
Okay.

133
00:07:12,850 --> 00:07:17,109
It gets dark at night, so you can use your phone’s light.

134
00:07:17,132 --> 00:07:19,911
That’s a great idea.

135
00:07:19,935 --> 00:07:23,226
Reviewing earthquake safety rules is really important.

136
00:07:23,250 --> 00:07:24,983
Okay.

137
00:07:25,006 --> 00:07:28,651
Let’s check them together from time to time.

138
00:07:28,674 --> 00:07:30,247
Okay.

139
00:07:30,270 --> 00:07:31,759
Let’s do that.

140
00:07:31,783 --> 00:07:33,283
Scene 4: Room Organization and Bookshelf Safety

141
00:07:33,283 --> 00:07:36,449
How do you like your new room?

142
00:07:36,472 --> 00:07:39,472
It’s so spacious!

143
00:07:39,495 --> 00:07:42,729
I love this room.

144
00:07:42,752 --> 00:07:46,885
Have you finished unpacking from the move?

145
00:07:46,908 --> 00:07:50,154
Yes, mostly done.

146
00:07:50,177 --> 00:07:52,711
Thanks for your help today.

147
00:07:52,734 --> 00:07:57,940
No problem. That bookshelf is really tall, though.

148
00:07:57,963 --> 00:08:03,011
Yeah, I have a lot of books.

149
00:08:03,035 --> 00:08:07,368
The bookshelf is right next to your bed, isn’t it?

150
00:08:07,391 --> 00:08:12,594
Yeah, I always read before bed.

151
00:08:12,618 --> 00:08:15,951
That’s a little dangerous, you know.

152
00:08:15,974 --> 00:08:17,832
Why?

153
00:08:17,856 --> 00:08:22,698
During a big earthquake, the bookshelf could fall over.

154
00:08:22,722 --> 00:08:24,955
Oh, right.

155
00:08:24,978 --> 00:08:30,229
It could fall onto your bed—very dangerous.

156
00:08:30,253 --> 00:08:33,219
That’s scary!

157
00:08:33,242 --> 00:08:35,499
What should I do?

158
00:08:35,523 --> 00:08:39,557
First, let’s move the bookshelf somewhere else.

159
00:08:39,580 --> 00:08:42,546
Okay. Where would be good?

160
00:08:42,569 --> 00:08:46,236
How about in front of that wall over there?

161
00:08:46,259 --> 00:08:48,192
Sounds good!

162
00:08:48,215 --> 00:08:50,487
Let's put it there.

163
00:08:50,510 --> 00:08:55,144
And let's secure the bookshelf firmly to the wall.

164
00:08:55,167 --> 00:08:58,133
How do we attach it to the wall?

165
00:08:58,156 --> 00:09:02,356
There are special tools for earthquakes.

166
00:09:02,379 --> 00:09:04,439
Oh, I see.

167
00:09:04,463 --> 00:09:07,334
Where can we find them?

168
00:09:07,357 --> 00:09:10,240
They're at the nearby supermarket.

169
00:09:10,264 --> 00:09:12,832
Are they expensive?

170
00:09:12,855 --> 00:09:15,937
No, they're quite affordable.

171
00:09:15,961 --> 00:09:18,127
Around 1,000 yen.

172
00:09:18,150 --> 00:09:20,841
That's a great deal!

173
00:09:20,865 --> 00:09:25,198
Let's go to the supermarket together to buy them now.

174
00:09:25,221 --> 00:09:27,454
Sure, let's go!

175
00:09:27,477 --> 00:09:30,644
Do you have any other large furniture?

176
00:09:30,667 --> 00:09:33,900
The TV is a bit big too.

177
00:09:33,923 --> 00:09:38,211
Then let's buy tools for the TV as well.

178
00:09:38,235 --> 00:09:40,124
Got it.

179
00:09:40,147 --> 00:09:44,680
Place heavy items on the lower shelves of the bookshelf.

180
00:09:44,703 --> 00:09:48,138
What should we put on the top shelves?

181
00:09:48,162 --> 00:09:51,095
Light items only, please.

182
00:09:51,118 --> 00:09:52,851
Got it.

183
00:09:52,874 --> 00:09:57,246
Earthquake preparedness is so important, isn't it?

184
00:09:57,270 --> 00:10:00,961
Yes, let's get everything done together today.

185
00:10:00,985 --> 00:10:04,385
Sounds good, I appreciate your help!

186
00:10:04,408 --> 00:10:05,908
Scene 5: Preparing an Emergency Bag

187
00:10:05,908 --> 00:10:08,797
What are you doing?

188
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:13,304
I'm preparing an emergency backpack.

189
00:10:13,327 --> 00:10:16,527
The bag for earthquakes, right?

190
00:10:16,550 --> 00:10:19,183
Yes, that's right.

191
00:10:19,206 --> 00:10:22,740
Today, I'll check what's inside.

192
00:10:22,763 --> 00:10:26,938
What's in the bag?

193
00:10:26,961 --> 00:10:30,599
There's water and food.

194
00:10:30,623 --> 00:10:33,656
How much water is there?

195
00:10:33,679 --> 00:10:38,812
Three 500-milliliter bottles.

196
00:10:38,835 --> 00:10:42,049
What kind of food?

197
00:10:42,073 --> 00:10:47,140
Long-lasting bread and chocolate.

198
00:10:47,163 --> 00:10:49,396
Chocolate is a great idea!

199
00:10:49,419 --> 00:10:52,236
What else is in there?

200
00:10:52,259 --> 00:10:55,826
Towels and clothes.

201
00:10:55,849 --> 00:10:58,582
Do you have a flashlight?

202
00:10:58,605 --> 00:11:01,481
Yes, here it is.

203
00:11:01,505 --> 00:11:04,305
Are the batteries new?

204
00:11:04,328 --> 00:11:08,534
Oh, the batteries are a bit old.

205
00:11:08,557 --> 00:11:13,032
We should replace them with new ones.

206
00:11:13,056 --> 00:11:14,823
I can imagine.

207
00:11:14,846 --> 00:11:18,612
I'll buy new batteries later.

208
00:11:18,635 --> 00:11:20,969
Do you have a radio too?

209
00:11:20,991 --> 00:11:24,559
Yes, there's a small radio.

210
00:11:24,583 --> 00:11:28,156
A phone charger is important too, right?

211
00:11:28,179 --> 00:11:31,912
Yes, I'll add a portable battery.

212
00:11:31,935 --> 00:11:35,190
Do you have any medicine or bandages?

213
00:11:35,214 --> 00:11:38,414
No, not yet.

214
00:11:38,437 --> 00:11:43,570
It's good to have medicine in case of injuries.

215
00:11:43,593 --> 00:11:45,567
Got it.

216
00:11:45,591 --> 00:11:49,191
I'll go to the pharmacy tomorrow to buy some.

217
00:11:49,214 --> 00:11:51,547
Is the bag heavy?

218
00:11:51,570 --> 00:11:56,241
It's a bit heavy, but I can still run.

219
00:11:56,265 --> 00:11:59,298
Where are you going to put that bag?

220
00:11:59,321 --> 00:12:02,188
I'll put it near the entrance.

221
00:12:02,211 --> 00:12:06,065
That's great because you can escape quickly.

222
00:12:06,089 --> 00:12:11,655
Right. Do you have an emergency bag at your place too?

223
00:12:11,678 --> 00:12:15,413
No, I haven't prepared one yet.

224
00:12:15,437 --> 00:12:20,437
Japan has a lot of earthquakes, so you should get ready.

225
00:12:20,460 --> 00:12:24,460
Yes, I'll prepare one this weekend.

226
00:12:24,483 --> 00:12:29,049
There’s a good emergency bag at the nearby supermarket.

227
00:12:29,072 --> 00:12:33,439
Could you show me the store this Sunday?

228
00:12:33,462 --> 00:12:36,495
Sure, let’s go together.

229
00:12:36,518 --> 00:12:38,018
Scene 6: Disaster Preparedness – Securing Water Supplies

230
00:12:38,018 --> 00:12:42,874
This is the disaster preparedness section at the supermarket, right?

231
00:12:42,897 --> 00:12:47,169
Yeah, there’s so much stuff here.

232
00:12:47,193 --> 00:12:51,040
Let’s start by buying water.

233
00:12:51,064 --> 00:12:52,864
I can imagine.

234
00:12:52,887 --> 00:12:56,487
Water is the most important.

235
00:12:56,510 --> 00:13:00,277
How much water do we need?

236
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:05,571
You need 3 liters per person per day.

237
00:13:05,595 --> 00:13:07,574
Oh, I see.

238
00:13:07,597 --> 00:13:11,131
How many days' worth should we buy?

239
00:13:11,154 --> 00:13:14,987
It’s best to get enough for 3 days.

240
00:13:15,010 --> 00:13:19,143
So that’s 9 liters per person.

241
00:13:19,166 --> 00:13:23,933
Right, 18 liters for two people.

242
00:13:23,956 --> 00:13:26,889
18 liters?

243
00:13:26,912 --> 00:13:29,989
That’s really heavy!

244
00:13:30,013 --> 00:13:34,379
No problem, we came by car today.

245
00:13:34,402 --> 00:13:36,436
That’s a relief.

246
00:13:36,459 --> 00:13:39,725
Let’s put this in the cart.

247
00:13:39,748 --> 00:13:42,548
Next up, food.

248
00:13:42,571 --> 00:13:46,105
We should get things that last long.

249
00:13:46,127 --> 00:13:48,294
What should we buy?

250
00:13:48,317 --> 00:13:51,357
How about canned food?

251
00:13:51,381 --> 00:13:53,114
Sounds good!

252
00:13:53,137 --> 00:13:55,393
Let’s buy a lot.

253
00:13:55,417 --> 00:13:59,150
Oh, they even have canned bread!

254
00:13:59,173 --> 00:14:00,340
Wait,

255
00:14:00,363 --> 00:14:03,541
There’s bread *inside* the can?

256
00:14:03,564 --> 00:14:07,498
Yeah, and it’s really tasty!

257
00:14:07,521 --> 00:14:09,722
That’s interesting!

258
00:14:09,745 --> 00:14:12,035
Let’s get this too.

259
00:14:12,059 --> 00:14:16,325
We should buy enough food for 3 days as well.

260
00:14:16,348 --> 00:14:18,148
Got it.

261
00:14:18,171 --> 00:14:20,705
They have curry too.

262
00:14:20,728 --> 00:14:25,814
Can you eat it without heating it up?

263
00:14:25,838 --> 00:14:29,471
Yes, the box says so.

264
00:14:29,494 --> 00:14:31,538
That’s convenient!

265
00:14:31,561 --> 00:14:33,828
Let’s get that too.

266
00:14:33,851 --> 00:14:37,855
Oh, we should grab some snacks too.

267
00:14:37,878 --> 00:14:40,045
Chocolate?

268
00:14:40,067 --> 00:14:45,201
Yeah, something sweet is good when you’re tired.

269
00:14:45,224 --> 00:14:46,990
I see.

270
00:14:47,013 --> 00:14:50,461
Then let’s get some chocolate and candy.

271
00:14:50,485 --> 00:14:54,052
Is there anything else we need?

272
00:14:54,075 --> 00:14:58,241
Should we get paper plates and cups too?

273
00:14:58,264 --> 00:15:00,333
Sounds good!

274
00:15:00,356 --> 00:15:03,399
It's really handy when the water stops.

275
00:15:03,423 --> 00:15:07,225
Yeah, because you don’t have to wash anything.

276
00:15:07,249 --> 00:15:11,182
Alright, let’s go check out that shelf over there.

277
00:15:11,205 --> 00:15:14,019
Sure, let's go!

278
00:15:14,043 --> 00:15:15,543
Scene 7: Evacuation Sites – What You Need to Know

279
00:15:15,543 --> 00:15:19,209
The weather’s lovely today, isn’t it?

280
00:15:19,232 --> 00:15:23,566
Yes, perfect for a walk!

281
00:15:23,589 --> 00:15:29,222
Oh, look—there’s a green sign over there.

282
00:15:29,245 --> 00:15:31,279
You’re right, there is!

283
00:15:31,303 --> 00:15:34,269
What does it say?

284
00:15:34,292 --> 00:15:37,585
It says ‘Evacuation Site.’

285
00:15:37,609 --> 00:15:40,243
An evacuation site?

286
00:15:40,266 --> 00:15:42,666
What’s that for?

287
00:15:42,688 --> 00:15:47,888
It’s where everyone goes during a big earthquake.

288
00:15:47,911 --> 00:15:50,278
Oh, I see.

289
00:15:50,301 --> 00:15:52,745
This is a park, right?

290
00:15:52,769 --> 00:15:58,775
Yes, and since it’s so spacious, it’s safe.

291
00:15:58,798 --> 00:16:03,836
There’s a sign like this near my house too.

292
00:16:03,859 --> 00:16:06,863
Where can we find them?

293
00:16:06,887 --> 00:16:10,820
It’s in front of the elementary school nearby.

294
00:16:10,843 --> 00:16:14,684
So schools can be evacuation sites too?

295
00:16:14,707 --> 00:16:19,949
Yes, that’s where I’d go if there’s an earthquake.

296
00:16:19,973 --> 00:16:23,412
That’s reassuring.

297
00:16:23,436 --> 00:16:29,494
But it gets dark at night—I’m a little worried.

298
00:16:29,517 --> 00:16:34,170
There’s a big road near this park.

299
00:16:34,193 --> 00:16:38,242
Yeah, that road is well-lit.

300
00:16:38,265 --> 00:16:43,332
If there’s an earthquake, walk on that bright road.

301
00:16:43,355 --> 00:16:45,569
Got it.

302
00:16:45,592 --> 00:16:48,398
Don’t walk on dark streets.

303
00:16:48,421 --> 00:16:52,193
Have you checked the map near your house?

304
00:16:52,217 --> 00:16:54,750
A map?

305
00:16:54,773 --> 00:16:58,352
No, I haven’t seen it yet.

306
00:16:58,376 --> 00:17:02,976
The town’s website has a hazard map.

307
00:17:02,998 --> 00:17:06,452
What’s a hazard map?

308
00:17:06,476 --> 00:17:10,443
It’s a map that shows dangerous areas.

309
00:17:10,466 --> 00:17:13,399
That’s really useful!

310
00:17:13,422 --> 00:17:17,556
Let’s look at that map together later.

311
00:17:17,579 --> 00:17:20,869
Yes, I’d love that!

312
00:17:20,893 --> 00:17:25,426
Alright, shall we walk around town a bit more?

313
00:17:25,449 --> 00:17:27,182
I can imagine.

314
00:17:27,205 --> 00:17:30,422
Let’s check out other signs too.

315
00:17:30,446 --> 00:17:33,012
Sure, let's go!

316
00:17:33,035 --> 00:17:34,535
Scene 8: Disaster Preparedness – Be Ready

317
00:17:34,535 --> 00:17:37,231
What are you doing?

318
00:17:37,255 --> 00:17:42,424
I’m charging my phone’s power bank.

319
00:17:42,448 --> 00:17:45,115
A power bank?

320
00:17:45,138 --> 00:17:47,305
Why?

321
00:17:47,328 --> 00:17:52,695
In case the power goes out during an earthquake.

322
00:17:52,718 --> 00:17:56,451
Oh, right—during a blackout.

323
00:17:56,474 --> 00:18:02,474
Yeah, if the power’s out, you can’t charge your phone.

324
00:18:02,497 --> 00:18:06,064
That would be a real problem.

325
00:18:06,086 --> 00:18:10,184
Exactly—you wouldn’t be able to contact family.

326
00:18:10,208 --> 00:18:13,975
Or check the news.

327
00:18:13,999 --> 00:18:18,999
Right, so I always keep it charged.

328
00:18:19,022 --> 00:18:23,189
How many power banks do you have?

329
00:18:23,212 --> 00:18:26,345
I have three.

330
00:18:26,368 --> 00:18:30,970
Three? That’s a lot!

331
00:18:30,993 --> 00:18:37,044
Yeah, because I also use a small fan besides my phone.

332
00:18:37,068 --> 00:18:41,350
Fans are essential in the summer, aren’t they?

333
00:18:41,373 --> 00:18:45,540
Yeah, we can't use the air conditioning.

334
00:18:45,563 --> 00:18:50,496
I have a portable power bank.

335
00:18:50,519 --> 00:18:53,929
Is the battery at 100%?

336
00:18:53,953 --> 00:18:58,119
No, it's not charging right now.

337
00:18:58,142 --> 00:19:00,316
That won't do.

338
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:03,427
Make sure to charge it today.

339
00:19:03,450 --> 00:19:07,850
Okay, I'll charge it as soon as I get home.

340
00:19:07,873 --> 00:19:13,407
What else do we need when the power goes out?

341
00:19:13,430 --> 00:19:17,563
Hmm, a flashlight, I guess.

342
00:19:17,586 --> 00:19:19,553
Exactly.

343
00:19:19,576 --> 00:19:22,242
It gets really dark at night.

344
00:19:22,265 --> 00:19:27,398
I'll stock up on extra batteries for the flashlight too.

345
00:19:27,421 --> 00:19:29,055
Sounds good!

346
00:19:29,078 --> 00:19:31,711
What about winter?

347
00:19:31,734 --> 00:19:36,534
If the power goes out in winter, it gets freezing cold.

348
00:19:36,557 --> 00:19:41,173
Right. I'll get out warm clothes and blankets.

349
00:19:41,197 --> 00:19:45,065
I'll also buy some hand warmers.

350
00:19:45,089 --> 00:19:47,627
That's a great idea.

351
00:19:47,650 --> 00:19:51,617
What do we do if the fridge stops working?

352
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:55,840
We should eat the food inside quickly.

353
00:19:55,863 --> 00:19:57,596
I can imagine.

354
00:19:57,619 --> 00:20:01,031
Because the food will spoil.

355
00:20:01,055 --> 00:20:04,188
Electricity is really important, isn't it?

356
00:20:04,211 --> 00:20:09,493
Yes. We should prepare a lot before an earthquake.

357
00:20:09,517 --> 00:20:12,211
Let's be careful together.

358
00:20:12,234 --> 00:20:13,734
Scene 9: The Ocean and Tsunami Risks / The Beauty and Dangers of the Sea: Tsunamis

359
00:20:13,734 --> 00:20:16,502
The ocean is so beautiful.

360
00:20:16,525 --> 00:20:19,858
Yes, it's really stunning.

361
00:20:19,881 --> 00:20:22,764
I love the ocean.

362
00:20:22,787 --> 00:20:24,962
Me too.

363
00:20:24,986 --> 00:20:28,619
But it's dangerous during an earthquake.

364
00:20:28,642 --> 00:20:30,461
Why?

365
00:20:30,485 --> 00:20:32,904
Because a tsunami could come.

366
00:20:32,927 --> 00:20:34,894
A tsunami?

367
00:20:34,917 --> 00:20:38,317
Yes, it's a huge wave.

368
00:20:38,340 --> 00:20:40,306
Really?

369
00:20:40,329 --> 00:20:44,696
Yes, it's an enormous and fast-moving wave.

370
00:20:44,719 --> 00:20:47,392
That sounds terrifying.

371
00:20:47,415 --> 00:20:53,249
It is. So after an earthquake, never go near the sea.

372
00:20:53,272 --> 00:20:55,110
Got it.

373
00:20:55,133 --> 00:20:57,346
What about rivers?

374
00:20:57,370 --> 00:20:59,624
Rivers are dangerous too.

375
00:20:59,647 --> 00:21:02,381
Don't go near rivers either.

376
00:21:02,404 --> 00:21:04,051
Oh, I see.

377
00:21:04,074 --> 00:21:07,041
Then where should we go?

378
00:21:07,064 --> 00:21:09,664
Head to higher ground.

379
00:21:09,687 --> 00:21:12,020
Higher ground, got it.

380
00:21:12,043 --> 00:21:14,610
Like where, for example?

381
00:21:14,633 --> 00:21:17,470
Tall buildings or mountains.

382
00:21:17,493 --> 00:21:19,186
Got it.

383
00:21:19,210 --> 00:21:21,844
Should we run quickly?

384
00:21:21,867 --> 00:21:24,633
Yes, run immediately.

385
00:21:24,656 --> 00:21:27,790
What about our belongings?

386
00:21:27,813 --> 00:21:30,979
Should we take an emergency bag?

387
00:21:31,002 --> 00:21:33,686
No, don't bring anything.

388
00:21:33,709 --> 00:21:37,243
But we'll struggle without supplies.

389
00:21:37,266 --> 00:21:40,799
But your life is the most important thing.

390
00:21:40,822 --> 00:21:44,029
Right. Got it.

391
00:21:44,053 --> 00:21:48,137
There's a tsunami warning sign near the ocean.

392
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:50,371
What kind of sign is it?

393
00:21:50,394 --> 00:21:53,649
It's a tsunami advisory sign.

394
00:21:53,673 --> 00:21:57,606
Oh, there it is!

395
00:21:57,629 --> 00:21:59,837
Yes, that's right.

396
00:21:59,861 --> 00:22:02,906
Are there any other signs?

397
00:22:02,929 --> 00:22:06,005
Yes, there's a blue sign too.

398
00:22:06,028 --> 00:22:08,562
What's the blue sign for?

399
00:22:08,585 --> 00:22:11,218
It's an evacuation site sign.

400
00:22:11,241 --> 00:22:13,374
An evacuation site?

401
00:22:13,397 --> 00:22:16,964
Yes, it's where everyone goes to stay safe.

402
00:22:16,987 --> 00:22:19,962
Over by that blue sign, right?

403
00:22:19,985 --> 00:22:23,678
That's right. That place is safe.

404
00:22:23,702 --> 00:22:28,268
When I walk near the ocean, I always check the signs.

405
00:22:28,291 --> 00:22:31,225
Yes, please be careful.

406
00:22:31,248 --> 00:22:32,748
Scene 10: Learning Kanji with News Apps

407
00:22:32,748 --> 00:22:36,081
You're looking at your phone.

408
00:22:36,104 --> 00:22:38,471
What are you doing?

409
00:22:38,494 --> 00:22:42,305
I'm reading Japanese news.

410
00:22:42,328 --> 00:22:46,294
But the kanji are so hard.

411
00:22:46,317 --> 00:22:48,727
Is it news about an earthquake?

412
00:22:48,751 --> 00:22:51,784
Yes, that's right.

413
00:22:51,807 --> 00:22:55,266
I want to read about this morning's earthquake.

414
00:22:55,289 --> 00:23:00,100
Want me to recommend a great app for that?

415
00:23:00,124 --> 00:23:01,858
An app?

416
00:23:01,881 --> 00:23:04,335
What kind of app is it?

417
00:23:04,358 --> 00:23:08,325
It's an app for news and weather.

418
00:23:08,348 --> 00:23:11,353
Is it a Japanese app?

419
00:23:11,376 --> 00:23:15,043
Yes, that's right.

420
00:23:15,066 --> 00:23:17,444
It's NHK's disaster prevention app.

421
00:23:17,467 --> 00:23:20,082
NHK?

422
00:23:20,106 --> 00:23:22,987
I often watch it on TV.

423
00:23:23,011 --> 00:23:26,786
This app is really useful!

424
00:23:26,809 --> 00:23:29,264
Why is it so useful?

425
00:23:29,288 --> 00:23:33,365
You can read the news in foreign languages.

426
00:23:33,388 --> 00:23:36,022
What? Really?

427
00:23:36,045 --> 00:23:37,724
Okay.

428
00:23:37,747 --> 00:23:41,617
There's English and other languages too.

429
00:23:41,641 --> 00:23:45,308
Is my language available?

430
00:23:45,331 --> 00:23:50,697
Yes, it supports many languages, so you'll be fine.

431
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:52,954
That's a great deal!

432
00:23:52,977 --> 00:23:56,210
Let me show you on my phone.

433
00:23:56,233 --> 00:23:58,433
Here it is.

434
00:23:58,456 --> 00:24:01,223
Oh, wow, it really is!

435
00:24:01,246 --> 00:24:05,012
I can read it in my own language!

436
00:24:05,035 --> 00:24:06,904
Right.

437
00:24:06,928 --> 00:24:11,928
When there's a big earthquake, you get alerts right away.

438
00:24:11,951 --> 00:24:15,006
That's really reassuring.

439
00:24:15,030 --> 00:24:19,231
You can also check the evacuation map.

440
00:24:19,255 --> 00:24:22,426
A map for where to go in an emergency?

441
00:24:22,450 --> 00:24:24,819
It's so convenient!

442
00:24:24,842 --> 00:24:26,417
Okay.

443
00:24:26,441 --> 00:24:29,459
It even warns you about tsunamis.

444
00:24:29,482 --> 00:24:35,049
I was always a little worried because I didn't understand the language.

445
00:24:35,072 --> 00:24:39,605
But with this app, you'll be fine now!

446
00:24:39,628 --> 00:24:42,807
I want this app too!

447
00:24:42,830 --> 00:24:47,109
Want to download it now?

448
00:24:47,133 --> 00:24:49,299
Yes, please!

449
00:24:49,322 --> 00:24:52,089
Does it cost anything?

450
00:24:52,112 --> 00:24:55,888
No, it doesn’t cost anything.

451
00:24:55,911 --> 00:24:57,845
It's completely free.

452
00:24:57,868 --> 00:24:59,714
That’s a relief.

453
00:24:59,737 --> 00:25:02,337
How do I install it?

454
00:25:02,360 --> 00:25:04,859
I’ll do it for you.

455
00:25:04,883 --> 00:25:07,450
Could you lend me your phone?

456
00:25:07,473 --> 00:25:10,039
Sure, thank you so much!

457
00:25:10,062 --> 00:25:12,396
All done!

458
00:25:12,419 --> 00:25:15,152
Now open the app.

459
00:25:15,175 --> 00:25:17,042
Okay.

460
00:25:17,065 --> 00:25:20,498
Oh, it switched to my language!

461
00:25:20,521 --> 00:25:22,696
That’s great, isn’t it?

462
00:25:22,719 --> 00:25:26,052
You’ve shown me such a useful app!

463
00:25:26,075 --> 00:25:28,675
I really appreciate it.

464
00:25:28,698 --> 00:25:33,698
No problem—just check the news every day, okay?

465
00:25:33,721 --> 00:25:36,321
Yes, I will!